[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"EVM Architecture and Gas Optimization"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM) is a quasi-Turing-complete state machine that executes smart contracts on the Ethereum blockchain. Understanding its internal architecture is crucial for writing secure and cost-effective smart contracts."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Components of EVM Architecture"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Stack Machine: The EVM is a stack-based machine with a maximum stack depth of 1024 items. Operations are performed by pushing and popping items from this stack."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Memory: A volatile, byte-array memory space that is expanded as needed during execution. Memory costs scale quadratically when usage exceeds certain thresholds."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Storage: A persistent, key-value store mapping 256-bit words to 256-bit words. Storage operations are the most expensive actions in the EVM."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Gas Costs"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Every operation executed by the EVM consumes a specific amount of gas to prevent infinite loops and denial-of-service attacks. Developers must optimize their code to minimize these costs."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"// Unoptimized Storage Pattern
contract Unoptimized {
    uint256 public a;
    uint256 public b;

    function update(uint256 _a, uint256 _b) public {
        a = _a;
        b = _b;
    }
}"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Gas Optimization Techniques"},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Variable Packing: Group state variables that take up less than 32 bytes into a single storage slot to save costly SSTORE operations."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use Custom Errors: Solidity custom errors consume significantly less gas than string-based require statements."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Memory vs Storage: Use memory or calldata for temporary variables instead of repeatedly reading from or writing to storage."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"// Optimized Storage Pattern using Packing
contract Optimized {
    uint128 public a;
    uint128 public b;

    function update(uint128 _a, uint128 _b) public {
        a = _a;
        b = _b;
    }
}"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"By mastering EVM architecture and applying targeted gas optimization strategies, developers can deploy highly efficient smart contracts that provide a better user experience and lower transaction fees."}]
